    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d958">

                <pb facs="1025" n="1015" xml:id="pg1015"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363/6–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-21T15:00:00+08:00">June 21, 1949—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 22—6:23 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2382. Navy Department SMCC<anchor n="33" xml:id="d958-f1"/> today published
                    notice <hi rendition="#italic">Liberation Daily</hi> freezing Caltex oil stocks
                    held for Kmt<anchor n="34" xml:id="d958-f2"/> armed services under Central Trust
                    contract at Nationalists’ risk and cancelled outstanding delivery orders. Prior
                    actual delivery, CalTex proposes request requisition orders from SMCC protect
                    its interests, which presumably obtainable without difficulty.</p>
                <p>As precaution avoid possible misunderstanding, please advise Caltex, New
                    York.</p>
                <p>Repeated Canton 761, Nanking 1270.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d958-f1" n="33" xml:id="d958-f1-content">
                <p>Shanghai Military Control Commission (Communist).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d958-f2" n="34" xml:id="d958-f2-content">
                <p>Kuomintang (Nationalist Party).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
